## Project context

This project spans two TypeScript + vitest codelines:

- **mocka** at `/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a` — source under `src/`, tests run via vitest. The expected change is a one-line logic fix in `src/fares.ts` where `fareFor` uses a strict-greater-than comparison that excludes riders aged exactly 65 from the adult fare. A reviewer should confirm the boundary condition is corrected (e.g. `>= 65` rather than `> 65`) and that a new test covering the exact age-65 case was added alongside the fix.
- **mockb** at `/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b` — source under `src/`, tests run via vitest. The expected change is a one-line logic fix in `src/schedule.ts` where `formatStops` iterates to `stops.length - 1` and drops the final stop. A reviewer should confirm the loop bound is corrected so the final stop is included and that a new test covering the last-stop case was added alongside the fix.

Both repos use TypeScript, so any signature change must remain type-safe. If the diff touches an exported function signature in either `src/fares.ts` or `src/schedule.ts`, flag it as API contract drift unless corresponding test updates are present in the same diff.

